Comment: This package builds the asmtest-desktop GUI application (desktop/), which
 links the GPL-2.0 Unicorn emulator and the BSD-3-Clause Keystone/Capstone engines
 directly. Because it conveys Unicorn as a binary dynamically linked into the app,
 the package as distributed is effectively GPL-2.0 as a whole, even though
 asm-test's own code (this source tree) is MIT. Unicorn/Keystone/Capstone are not
 part of this source package — they are built from pinned upstream source at
 package-build time (scripts/build-keystone.sh, scripts/build-capstone.sh; Unicorn
 itself from the libunicorn-dev Build-Depends) and vendored privately under
 /usr/lib/asmtest-desktop/, with their exact-version license texts reproduced under
 /usr/share/doc/asmtest-desktop/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/ (scripts/collect-licenses.sh).
 The desktop app also statically compiles in Dear ImGui and nlohmann-json (both
 MIT) and a handful of small permissively-licensed ImGui addons — see
 licenses/README.md upstream for the full inventory; none is separately copyright
 here since none is a Debian dependency.

